From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: domicile CI <ci@domicile.invalid>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: a touchpad rests while the keyboard types

A palm on the pad while typing moved the pointer and tapped. libinput has
disable-while-typing, but it pairs a pad with a keyboard only inside one
libinput context, and evdev opens each device in its own: keyboards go to
`EventConverterEvdevImpl` and never reach libinput at all.

- `TypingGuard` (`domicile/typing_guard.{h,cc}`) holds the rule, with
  libinput's timeouts: one key rests the pads 200 ms, typing 500 ms.
  Modifiers, keys past F1 and Ctrl/Alt/Super shortcuts rest nothing. A
  release goes the way its press went, and a held button keeps motion
  passing.
- `InputDeviceFactoryEvdev` owns one and hands it to every converter
  (`EventConverterEvdev::SetTypingGuard`). A keyboard reports its keys; a
  libinput touchpad drops motion, scrolls and buttons it says to.
- On by default. `InputDeviceSettingsEvdev::domicile_disable_while_typing`
  carries the switch to the evdev thread, set through
  `InputControllerEvdev` and `OzonePlatform::SetDomicileDisableWhileTyping`,
  which the command socket's `disable_while_typing` calls.
- `typing_guard_unittest.cc` runs in ozone_unittests.

Verified: not built. This repository cannot build Chromium; the engine
job builds it on `crux`.
